  "result": "All 8 tests pass, including the three new ones in tests/test_t2.py.\n\n**What I changed** in `ledger/ledger.py` (the existing snapshot-state design, Approach B):\n\n- **apply_interest(basis_points)** iterates the balance dict and credits each positive balance with `balance * bp // 10000`, so interest is floored to whole cents. Zero balances are skipped. Negative or non-int basis points raise ValueError via the existing amount validator.\n- **close_account(id)** looks up the account (raising UnknownAccount if missing), raises ValueError if the balance is not exactly zero, and otherwise deletes the entry. The id then behaves as unknown to balance and accounts.\n- **total_assets()** returns the sum of all balances.\n\nNo files under tests/ were modified.",
